Id: time006w
Severity: WARN
Category: services
Check: check_timesync
Fix: Find whether the named source is wrong, then drop or replace it.
References: chronyc(1); ntp.conf(5)
Controls: CIS 8.4; NIST AU-8, SC-45; ISO 8.17

The time daemon calls the named source a falseticker: its time
disagrees with the other sources, so the daemon does not use it.
Usually the source's own clock is failing, but a source fed false
time on purpose looks the same. Find which it is, then drop or
replace that source.
